/tmp/paper_1504_src/vor-diagrams.tex:17:This is a contradiction with the definition of normality.
/tmp/paper_1504_src/vor-diagrams.tex:23:Suppose $\Fam\subseteq \Obj$ is a normal subfamily of objects and let $\Vorpar=\Vorpar_\Fam$ be the Voronoi partition w.r.t. $\Fam$. Then for every $p\in \Fam$ and every $v\in \Vorpar(p)$, the unique shortest path from $v$ to $\loc(p)$ is entirely contained in $\Vorpar(p)$. In particular, $G[\Vorpar(p)]$ is connected.
