The construction decision is Track B, not Track A. I’ll use the paper’s Section 6.1 parabola construction verbatim at the object level: clients are exact rational points and every candidate is a closed convex polygon defined by its parabola vertices. The planted cover is sampled first. Its boundary incidences compose affine permutations, giving a short certificate-carrying route; the honest mechanical solver enumerates and propagates all residue choices. This preserves the paper’s geometry while making the algorithmic shortcut—and its cost—explicit.
