+NOTES = (
+    "Section 3.1 fixes the paper's general problem, including its exact-k "
+    "condition and normality requirement.  The generated family instead uses "
+    "the native convex-polygon covering problem of Section 6.1: Theorem 1.8's "
+    "proof places clients p_j=(j(N+1),j^2) on a parabola and observes that a "
+    "convex polygon through any chosen subset covers exactly that subset.  "
+    "The positive n^{O(sqrt(k))} results for disks and squares do not extend "
+    "to arbitrary convex polygons; Theorem 1.8 gives an n^{k-o(1)} SETH lower "
+    "bound for the general family.  This particular distribution is Track B, "
+    "because its affine boundary maps admit an O(kn) propagation algorithm.  "
+    "Generation samples the k selected polygons first, samples nonzero affine "
+    "slopes with nonunit cyclic product, and sets each intercept so the sampled "
+    "polygons cover.  Equal polygon vertex counts defeat size outliers; random "
+    "affine maps defeat fixed-label and arithmetic-progression guesses; the "
+    "unique cyclic fixed point defeats greedy start-zero propagation and random "
+    "full-tuple restarts."
