codex
Step 0 found a stronger native family than the initial packing idea: Section 7 proves ETH-hardness for covering two tracks of points with closed interval pairs, via a certificate-preserving reduction from Partitioned Subgraph Isomorphism with a 3-regular bipartite pattern. Ordinary one-track covering is polynomial-time—the paper explicitly identifies that easy boundary—while the two-track regime has no \(f(k)N^{o(k/\log k)}\) algorithm under ETH. I’m testing a planted, degree-balanced version of that exact construction now; degree balancing is important because it removes the usual planted-vertex outlier.
