The first balanced planted distribution was not acceptable: a maintained-arc-consistency backtracker solved every tested instance in only a few to hundreds of search nodes. That is exactly the Step 0 discriminator in practice, so I’m not treating the paper’s worst-case theorem as distributional evidence. I’m stress-testing the theorem’s hard regime with a larger fixed witness and a growing ambient label space; if the standard solver remains cheap, I’ll reject this route rather than hide it behind the ETH statement.
