The paper supports a viable Track B family, not Track A: unrestricted convex-polygon covering has the paper’s SETH lower bound, but this generator’s affine-cycle distribution has an explicit \(O(kn)\) propagation solver. The useful benchmark gap is roughly 36,000 mechanical table operations versus about 200 arithmetic operations after recognizing the affine invariant. I’m now auditing whether the existing module reports that gap and its geometry honestly.
